          },
          "code": "GENERATE_INITIAL_INFO_DISPLAYS",
          "id": "1769721577282",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769721577283_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Strategic Cross-Sell Enablement. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\n\nDATA: {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_THE_CONTENT_TYPES.$output.result}}\n\nDIRECTIVE: First, analyze the input data and determine what will populate the oraInfoDisplay XML block. Then generate a concise, business-ready text summary that introduces and contextualizes the widget content. Finally, output the oraInfoDisplay XML block using the messageListWidget pattern.\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n1. text: Before generating the widget, write 1-2 executive-level sentences that clearly convey the value of the information that will be displayed, focusing on enabling actionable insights, data-driven decisions, increased agility, and superior business outcomes. This text should naturally lead into the widget content. Do not mention \"content types,\" UI, widgets, or similar references.\n2. title: Generate an impactful, professional headline for {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}} with an emphasis on data-driven insights, accelerated decision-making, and business impact. Use sentence case only; avoid all caps.\n3. description: If used, ensure it adds context to the headline, maintaining a results-driven, strategic tone.\n\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n- For messageListWidget:\n  - items[].title: Map from the Name or name attribute in the data.\n  - items[].summary: Generate a one-line professional sentence based on the Description or description attribute in the data, and include the exact record count from recordCount in natural language, for example \"12 records available.\" If recordCount is 0, state that no records are currently available.\n  - If the widget supports a subtitle or badge text for list items, use recordCount there as \"<recordCount>\" while still preserving a concise summary.\n\nACTION LOGIC:\nFor each item, set action to ora.Invoke(\"launchContent\", \"targetProductName=<targetProductName>,contentContext=<referenceKey>\") with <referenceKey> from the item's referenceKey and <targetProductName> from {{$context.$variables.targetProductName}}. Do not include any quotation marks around parameter names or values.\n\nOUTPUT ORDER:\n1. Output the text first (the 1-2 sentence executive summary)\n2. Then output the oraInfoDisplay XML block\n\nEnsure all written content is generic, outcome-focused, and avoids referencing lists, displays, or content types."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Refine the Content Types",
            "sourceCode": "let result = [];\ntry {\n  const contentTypes = $context.$nodes?.GET_CONTENT_TYPES?.$output?.items || [];\n  let countResults = $context.$variables?.contentTypeCounts || [];\n\n  if (typeof countResults === \"string\") {\n    try {\n      countResults = JSON.parse(countResults);\n    } catch (parseError) {\n      countResults = [];\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (!Array.isArray(countResults)) {\n    countResults = [];\n  }\n\n  const normalize = value => String(value ?? \"\").trim().toLowerCase();\n  const countsByContentType = countResults.reduce((acc, item) => {\n    const keys = [\n      item?.referenceKey,\n      item?.name,\n      item?.Name,\n      item?.contentType,\n      item?.contentTypeCode\n    ].map(normalize).filter(Boolean);\n    const recordCount = Number(item?.recordCount ?? item?.count ?? 0);\n\n    keys.forEach(key => {\n      acc[key] = Math.max(acc[key] || 0, Number.isFinite(recordCount) ? recordCount : 0);\n    });\n    return acc;\n  }, {});\n\n  result = [...contentTypes]\n    .map(contentType => {\n      const keys = [\n        contentType?.referenceKey,\n        contentType?.name,\n        contentType?.Name,\n        contentType?.contentType,\n        contentType?.contentTypeCode\n      ].map(normalize).filter(Boolean);\n\n      const recordCount = keys.reduce((count, key) => Math.max(count, countsByContentType[key] || 0), 0);\n\n      return {\n        ...contentType,\n        recordCount\n      };\n    })\n    .sort((a, b) => {\n      const nameA = a?.name || a?.Name || \"\";\n      const nameB = b?.name || b?.Name || \"\";\n      if (nameA > nameB) return 1;\n      if (nameA < nameB) return -1;\n      return 0;\n    });\n} catch (error) {\n  result = [];\n}\nreturn result;",
            "returnType": "array"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5150,
            "y": 7036
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769714845784"
          },
          "id": "1778728253975",
          "code": "REFINE_THE_CONTENT_TYPES",
          "type": "CODE",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}"
